oyo a la higiene dental durante la masticación\n\n**Instrucciones de alimentación**\nOfrecer 1 unidad 2-3 veces por semana como premio o entretenimiento. No sustituye a una dieta equilibrada. El pelo ayuda al tránsito, pero no desparasita: no sustituye al desparasitante veterinario.\n\n**Conservación y uso responsable**\n- Guarda la bolsa en un lugar fresco y seco, bien cerrada después de cada uso\n- No llevan conservantes: evita la humedad y consúmelas dentro del periodo indicado en el envase\n- Supervisa la masticación, especialmente con perros que tragan sin desmenuzar\n- Ten siempre agua fresca a su alcance\n\n**Composición analítica**\n- Proteína bruta: 66,0%\n- Grasa bruta: 18,5%\n- Fibra bruta: 2,5%\n- Ceniza bruta: 7,9%\n- Humedad: 5,0%	**Wild deer ear, slowly dehydrated** with its natural hair on. It's processed whole, just as it comes from the animal, and the hair acts as *insoluble fibre* that mechanically supports intestinal transit and adds bulk to stools. A lean, single-protein chew made from *novel protein*, suitable for dogs with sensitivities. Its moderate chew supports dental hygiene.\n\nBeing lean, it's a good alternative to pig ears for dogs on weight control or that don't digest fat well. The first few times, the hair may loosen stools slightly: that's normal.\n\n**Single protein, grain-free, no additives or preservatives. High in protein, low in fat.**\n\n**Ingredients:** 100% wild deer ear with hair. No additives, preservatives or colourings.\n\n**Origin:** Toledo, Spain. Made in Catalonia.\n\n**Size:** 3 pieces.\n\n**Suitable for**\n- Dog size: small, medium and large\n- Hardness: 3 out of 5, crunchy\n- Lasts: long-lasting, 15 minutes or more\n- Sensitive dogs: if you're coming from an elimination diet, introduce it on its own for a few days before adding anything else\n\n**When to give them**\n- As a source of natural fibre for intestinal transit\n- For dogs with sensitivities or food intolerances: venison is a novel, single protein\n- As a 