do. La pieza reparada no pierde valor; cambia su significado. Se vuelve única.\n\nKintsugi no busca perfección. Busca honestidad.\n\nY en esas líneas doradas, lo que se rompió… encuentra otra forma de permanecer.\n\n**Características:**\n\n- Vela en envase de vidrio negro con tapa personalizada Komorebi artesanal.\n- 210 g de cera de soja sin parafinas.\n- Pabilo de algodón.\n- Esencias premium veganas, libres de ftalatos y parabenos, y certificadas por IFRA.\n- Opción con caja personalizada de la marca (ideal para regalar o regalarte).\n- Ideal para las y los amantes de la cultura japonesa.\n\n**Pirámide olfativa:**\n\n- **Notas altas:** albaricoque y nectarina.\n- **Notas medias:** osmanthus.\n- **Notas de fondo:** crema de vainilla.	*Kintsugi…* "repairing with gold", or the art of loving our scars and coming back stronger.\n\nIt was born in Japan as a technique for restoring broken ceramics, but its meaning goes beyond the object. It doesn't hide the cracks: it traces them with gold, makes them visible, makes them part of the piece.\n\nKintsugi is that gesture. It is not returning to the original state. It is not erasing the damage. It is transforming it.\n\nEvery fracture tells a story. Instead of being disguised, it is recognised as part of the journey. The repaired piece doesn't lose value; its meaning changes. It becomes unique.\n\nKintsugi doesn't seek perfection. It seeks honesty.\n\nAnd in those golden lines, what was broken… finds another way to last.\n\n**Features:**\n\n- Candle in a black glass jar with a custom Komorebi artesanal lid.\n- 210 g of paraffin-free soy wax.\n- Cotton wick.\n- Vegan premium essences, free from phthalates and parabens, and IFRA-certified.\n- Option with the brand's custom gift box (ideal as a gift, or a treat for yourself).\n- Ideal for lovers of Japanese culture.\n\n**Fragrance pyramid:**\n\n- **Top notes:** apricot and nectarine.\n- **Middle notes:** osmanthus.\n- **Base notes:** vanilla cream.	Komorebi artesanal	20.25	\N	2